{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465363-v5-baali-homebrew-book-review-issues","id":1465363,"title":"v5 Baali homebrew book...review/issues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-26T00:36:19-07:00","id":1465363,"title":"v5 Baali homebrew book...review/issues","content":"So im not sure about the clan baali guide.... its fandmade and looks highly professional. First impression - wow this could acutally be an official thing. However there is some issues with the book that i just want to mention as suggestion for improvement.<br /> <br /> 1) Clan Bane: Double damage from true faith, gains repelled by (holy symbols) like the folcloric bane. Issue: How do you then explain the Baalis presence in the church hierarchy up to cardinal?<br /> Problem 2: Doesnt take into account severity of the curse / bloot power at all.<br /> <br /> Solution: gain a +X dice penalty, depending on severity of the curse, on any action on &quot;holy ground&quot; or acting against someone / thing with true faith. Gain +x damage from true faith that cant be soaked.<br /> <br /> 2) Humanity....now that will be its own topic cause really, The Tzimisce and in this book the Baali gained an ability that basicly allows them to cheat their way out of consequences for their actions. You caaaan do it but the paths, while more confusing and complex, at leat make sure you actually have to adhear to some tennets<br /> <br /> 3) Discipline. Given how presence works in v5, shares abilities with daimonion and that dark thaumaturgy would be integrated into blood magic, id change the clan disciplines to obfuscate, daimonion and blood sorcery, making the dark thaumaturgy paths into choosable points instead of the standard powers.<br /> <br /> Daimonion 1: Overall well done but maybe replace the OR with AND. so at 5 net successes you get all these informations not just one. Remember it can be resistet.<br /> Since it is also the signature move for Baali AND prerequisite to further powers id remove the rouse check. You can do the same thing with auspex for free.<br /> <br /> Daimonion 2: can stay as is<br /> <br /> So Daimonion 3 dots. 3 dots is quite a bit to gain and you get....1 aggravated damage...that you have to aim and hit...and can be dodged. I am underwhelmed. If you can use the normal dodge rules it should do damage based on net hits. So i roll 4 successes, the enemy dodges with 2 successes - takes 2 aggravated damage. Sounds better to me at least specially given in the current state id have to make 1 rouse check per shot...<br /> <br /> Daimonion 4 &amp; 5: I am overall fine with but just one rouse check? Id increase that to 2 for the 4 ppower and 3 checks for the level 5 power given it can really weaken an opponent severly...and for weeks or longer...<br /> <br /> Dark thaumaturgy:<br /> <br /> First, it was stated at least in v20, that vampires cant use sorcery anymore (just like they loose the ability to use true magick if they were awakened) but they can use thaumaturgy instead. Hence, i wouldnt classify dark thaumaturgy as &quot;sorcery&quot; but actually integrate it as options for blood sorcery, the discipline<br /> <br /> Second, id add a lot more optional powers from official dark thaumaturgy paths before jumping to rituals<br /> <br /> As example you can take all the official paths as they are, also system wise and just change bloodpoint cost with rouse checks and you got a lot of options to add to the discipline depending if you do path of phobos, pleasure, pain etc. In special path of the unspoken can be used very well to disguise yourself as malkavian.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 10-26-2021, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T00:42:55-07:00","id":1465365,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of really good material in the Storyteller's Vault but there's always going to be issues. I'm debating making an official thread for discussing Storyteller's Vault products and fan content.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T01:16:26-07:00","id":1465369,"title":"","content":"I'll point out that Daimoinon 1 and 2 already exist in V5 as a Cult of Shalim merit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Crush the Dreams of Life:</b><br /> <br /> Shalim\u2019s teachings say the dreams and ambitions of the flesh must be cast-off to achieve perfection. All are equal under its gaze and so all must witness the path to the glorious dark of emptiness through the felling of their conceited ambition.<br /> <br /> When you succeed on an Insight roll against any character, the Storyteller reveals to you their foremost ambition in addition to the information sought by the roll. Armed with this knowledge, you may now reroll any dice in a failed Persuasion roll per scene against them as you turn their desires to your advantage. Furthermore, you may choose to roll Manipulation + Persuasion against the difficulty of the target\u2019s Composure + Insight. If you succeed, you crush their hopes and dreams, plunging them into despair and inaction for the remainder of the story in the form of one Aggravated Willpower damage. A total failure exposes your ruse and turns them against you. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T07:58:41-07:00","id":1465401,"title":"","content":"For the Bane, how does this look?<br /> <br /> Profane Presence: Baali blood is tainted by the infernal. You know, therefore, that there are higher powers in the universe than mere vampires, despite any cynicism you may profess. Whenever you are faced by a person with True Faith, you add your Bane Severity to any damage they inflict upon you (before soak). Furthermore, if they wield a symbol of faith, they may hold you at bay with ease -- you must keep a minimum distance between you and the icon of one metre per dot of True Faith. You must make a Willpower test to either come closer than this or to avoid fleeing if you are already within this range. The difficulty is equal to your Bane Severity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T09:01:31-07:00","id":1465409,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers =)<br /> <br /> i noticed another issue. Most powers are rolled attribute+discipline. In the case of daimonion most powers are rolled with occult+daimonion.<br /> <br /> Should that be changed? Would specialsiation (bloodmagic or infernalism) apply to power usage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T09:19:58-07:00","id":1465412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465363-v5-baali-homebrew-book-review-issues?p=1465409#post1465409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers =)<br /> <br /> i noticed another issue. Most powers are rolled attribute+discipline. In the case of daimonion most powers are rolled with occult+daimonion.<br /> <br /> Should that be changed? Would specialsiation (bloodmagic or infernalism) apply to power usage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think their whole take on the Discipline was ill conceived. Too focused on trying to make the Baali work like in V20 instead of fully integrating them on V5.<br /> <br /> Take the proper V5 route and make them powers or combinations for existing Disciplines. As thematic as Daimonion is, it isn't anything that can't work that way, and this will actually give you clearer ideas on how to correct anything you don't agree with their take on.<br /> <br /> And for Baal's sake, yes, ignore the Occult thing and roll with an Attribute. All the occult knowledge relevant to the task is already in your Discipline rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T12:09:39-07:00","id":1465430,"title":"","content":"Is this another take on Baali in V5? It seems they give Oblivion to the Baali, which honestly seems a good idea. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/375095\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/img/stvault/m_icon_menu_cab.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/375095\" target=\"_blank\"> Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/375095\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/375095 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> wot pdf, nwod pdf, download wod, white wolf, ww, wod, nwod, vtm, mta, mage the ascension, world of darkness, drivethru, rpg, roleplaying, role-playing, role playing, tabletop, rules, adventure, Changeling, Werewolf, Recoking, Masquerade, vtm, Vampire, pdf </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T12:16:06-07:00","id":1465431,"title":"","content":"My opinion is that the Baali are better off fully converted into a cult rather than a vampiric bloodline. Here's my (very rough) draft of a Baali loresheet.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Unaussprechlichen Kulten.</b> For millennia the Baali have cultivated the paradigms and cults to serve their dark masters. As a Baali yourself, you can partake of their services. Gain Status (Infernalists) \u25cf that applies to any and all infernalists.</li> <li><b>In Azaneal's Footsteps.</b> Following the teachings of a great shaitan, you have tamed your Beast, leashing it to the needs of the Masters Below. Stains from all actions done in service to the Baali or Infernal agenda are reduced by one, to the minimum of zero.</li> <li><b>Sense the Sin.</b> [Cult of Shalim 4 is already Sense the Sin + Fear of the Void Below, we are going to reuse it.]</li> <li><b>Lure Diabolic.</b> It is one thing to force the victim to its knees. It is completely different to let them descend on their own. You can push any being, mortal or otherwise, to indulge in degenerative corruption. With a successful Manipulation + Persuasion roll, you can persuade any individual to break a Tenet or Conviction, gaining at least one Stain. When it is done, the difficulty of Social checks against the victim is reduced by one until the end of the story.</li> <li><b>Condemnation.</b> The power of cursing is the pinnacle of the dark arts of the Baali, and you have studied rigorously. Though you can not doom entire bloodlines like the Baali of old, you have harnessed enough infernal taint to doom a few individuals. Once per story, you can make a Resolve + Composure check to lay a curse on a person. No successes indicate mild annoyance, like the loss of a Background dot, while 4 or more mean crippling doom such as the impotence of vitae or use of all dice as hunger dice in every roll. The Baali can reverse this curse at any time they wish, though they will likely demand a high price. The Baali's death does not lift the curse, but at the Storyteller's discretion, a spiritual quest and divine absolution might.</li> </ol> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T13:35:11-07:00","id":1465433,"title":"","content":"It is different yes. I decided my approach will be to integrate dark thaumaturgy and daimonion into Blood sorcery as alternate powers to choose from and replace daimonion with blood sorcery<br /> <br /> Azaneali would get oblivion ofc, i dont think it really fits standard Baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T13:50:56-07:00","id":1465434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465363-v5-baali-homebrew-book-review-issues?p=1465430#post1465430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this another take on Baali in V5? It seems they give Oblivion to the Baali, which honestly seems a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oblivion doesn't seems like a good idea by itself, but that's another rant.<br /> <br /> Baali don't actually work with powers similar to Oblivion. Daimoinon is clearly a combination of Auspex, Dominate and Thaumaturgy. It have to do with the theme of infernalism, but not with actual demonic contact most of the time, since the Baali threads the demonic contact with actual Investments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}